Customer Churn Analysis and Prediction
Student: Aman Mishra
Institution: United University, Prayagraj
Program: IBM SkillsBuild Data Analytics with AI Academic Internship 2026

Project Overview
This project analyzes customer churn using the IBM Telco Customer Churn sample dataset. The workflow includes data cleaning, exploratory data analysis (EDA), visualization, feature preprocessing, Logistic Regression, Decision Tree classification, model evaluation, and business-oriented interpretation.

Dataset
Dataset: IBM Telco Customer Churn sample dataset
Rows: 7,043 customers
Columns: 21
Target: Churn

Dataset URL:
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IBM/telco-customer-churn-on-icp4d/master/data/Telco-Customer-Churn.csv

Technologies Used
Python
Pandas
NumPy
Matplotlib
Seaborn
Scikit-learn
Jupyter Notebook
Project Workflow
Load dataset
Inspect structure and missing values
Clean and convert TotalCharges
Remove duplicate customer IDs
Perform EDA
Analyze churn by contract, internet service, payment method and tenure
Visualize numerical relationships
Encode categorical variables
Train Logistic Regression
Train Decision Tree
Evaluate accuracy, precision, recall, F1 and ROC-AUC
Generate business-oriented insights
How to Run
Install dependencies:

pip install -r requirements.txt
Start Jupyter:

jupyter notebook
Open AmanMishra_CustomerChurnAnalysis.ipynb and run all cells from top to bottom.

The notebook downloads the public dataset directly from the IBM GitHub source when it is executed.

Notes
This is an educational/academic analytics project.
The dataset is a public sample dataset, not a live telecom customer database.
Model predictions should not be treated as production decisions without further validation, monitoring and fairness assessment.